::ENG3_U05_L02_Q01::[MLA.ENG3.V.02] Sentence: The inscription on the monument listed the names of workers. Root clue: script means write. What does inscription mean? {
~A spoken warning#The root and context point to writing, not speech.
~A hidden emotion#This is not connected to the root or context.
=Words written or carved on something#Correct. Script means write, and a monument can carry written names.
~A public celebration#This is not supported by the word part.
}
::ENG3_U05_L02_Q02::[MLA.ENG3.V.02] Sentence: The final line was barely audible from the back row. Related word: audio. What does audible mean? {
~Able to be trusted#This connects to credible, not audio.
=Able to be heard#Correct. Audio connects to sound and hearing.
~Able to be carried#This connects to port.
~Able to be seen#This connects to vis.
}
::ENG3_U05_L02_Q03::[MLA.ENG3.V.02] Word family: portable, transport, import, export. What does port most likely mean? {
=Carry or move#Correct. The word family connects to carrying or moving.
~Write or mark#This connects to script.
~Hear or sound#This connects to audio.
~Trust or believe#This connects to cred.
}
::ENG3_U05_L02_Q04::[MLA.ENG3.R.10] Sentence: The critic questioned the credibility of the source. Which paraphrase is best? {
~The critic asked whether the source was colorful.#This does not match credibility.
~The critic asked whether the source was old.#This is not the meaning.
~The critic asked whether the source was printed.#This adds an unsupported detail.
=The critic asked whether the source could be trusted.#Correct. Credibility means trustworthiness.
}
::ENG3_U05_L02_Q05::[MLA.ENG3.V.01] Context: Choose the sentence that uses visible correctly. {
~The visible of the claim was unclear.#Visible is not used correctly as a noun here.
=The chart made the pattern visible to readers.#Correct. Visible means able to be seen or understood.
~The speaker visible the evidence.#Visible is not a verb here.
~The visible audience listened.#This is awkward and unclear.
}
::ENG3_U05_L02_Q06::[MLA.ENG3.V.02] Sentence: The author revised the paragraph after receiving feedback. Root clue: vis means see; re- means again. What does revised mean here? {
~Carried away#This connects to port, not revise.
~Heard clearly#This connects to audio, not revise.
=Looked at again and changed#Correct. Re- plus vis supports seeing again, and context supports changing writing.
~Trusted completely#This connects to cred, not revise.
}
::ENG3_U05_L02_Q07::[MLA.ENG3.V.02] Word family: credible, credit, credibility, incredible. What idea connects these words? {
~Sound#This connects to audio.
~Writing#This connects to script.
~Carrying#This connects to port.
=Belief or trust#Correct. The word family connects to trust and believability.
}
::ENG3_U05_L02_Q08::[MLA.ENG3.R.10] Sentence: The speaker's claim was incredible because it lacked evidence. Which paraphrase best uses word-family knowledge? {
~The claim was easy to carry because it lacked evidence.#This misuses the word family.
=The claim was hard to believe because it lacked evidence.#Correct. Incredible can mean difficult to believe.
~The claim was easy to hear because it lacked evidence.#This confuses incredible with audible.
~The claim was written because it lacked evidence.#This confuses the root with script.
}
::ENG3_U05_L02_Q09::[MLA.ENG3.V.02] Sentence: The portable recorder helped the student capture the interview. Root clue: port means carry. What does portable mean? {
=Easy to carry or move#Correct. Port supports carry, and the context supports a movable recorder.
~Able to be heard#This connects to audio.
~Able to be trusted#This connects to credible.
~Written on a surface#This connects to inscription.
}
::ENG3_U05_L02_Q10::[MLA.ENG3.V.01] Context: Choose the sentence that uses credibility correctly. {
~The credibility was blue and visible.#This does not use the word meaningfully.
=The speaker improved credibility by citing reliable evidence.#Correct. Credibility means trustworthiness.
~The student carried the credibility to class.#This confuses credibility with a physical object.
~The audience heard credibility from the hallway.#This misuses the word.
}
::ENG3_U05_L02_Q11::[MLA.ENG3.V.02] Word family: visual, visible, vision, revise. Which root meaning connects the words? {
~Carry#This connects to port.
~Write#This connects to script.
=See#Correct. Vis connects to seeing.
~Trust#This connects to cred.
}
::ENG3_U05_L02_Q12::[MLA.ENG3.R.10] Sentence: The visual evidence clarified the trend. Which paraphrase is best? {
=The evidence that could be seen made the trend clearer.#Correct. Visual connects to seeing.
~The evidence that could be heard made the trend clearer.#This confuses visual with audio.
~The evidence that could be carried made the trend clearer.#This confuses visual with portable.
~The evidence that could be trusted made the trend clearer.#This shifts to credible.
}
::ENG3_U05_L02_Q13::[MLA.ENG3.V.02] Sentence: The manuscript contained early notes from the author. Root clue: script means write. What is a manuscript? {
~A spoken recording#This is not connected to script.
~A tool for carrying papers#This connects to carry, not writing.
=A written document or draft#Correct. Script means write, and the context mentions notes.
~A visual chart#This connects more to seeing than writing.
}
::ENG3_U05_L02_Q14::[MLA.ENG3.V.02] Prefix clue: pre- means before. Sentence: The teacher asked students to preview the text. What does preview mean? {
~Carry the text away#This is not supported by pre- or view.
~Trust the text completely#This is not supported by the word parts.
~Write the text again#This is not supported by pre- or view.
=Look at the text before reading closely#Correct. Pre- means before, and view connects to seeing.
}
::ENG3_U05_L02_Q15::[MLA.ENG3.V.01] Context: Choose the sentence that uses etymology correctly. {
=Etymology can help readers use word origins to predict meaning.#Correct. This accurately uses the word.
~Etymology means a sentence has correct punctuation.#This defines conventions, not etymology.
~Etymology is a type of paragraph conclusion.#This is incorrect.
~Etymology means a word has no history.#This contradicts the meaning.
}
::ENG3_U05_L02_Q16::[MLA.ENG3.V.02] Sentence: The transcript recorded every question from the interview. Root clue: script means write. What does transcript mean? {
~A spoken guess#This does not match the root or context.
=A written record of spoken words#Correct. Script supports writing, and the interview context supports recorded speech.
~A portable device#This connects to port.
~A visible drawing#This connects to vis.
}
::ENG3_U05_L02_Q17::[MLA.ENG3.R.10] Sentence: The portable exhibit moved from school to school. Which paraphrase is best? {
~The trusted exhibit moved from school to school.#Portable does not mean trusted.
~The written exhibit moved from school to school.#Portable does not mean written.
~The audible exhibit moved from school to school.#Portable does not mean audible.
=The exhibit could be carried or moved from one school to another.#Correct. Portable means able to be carried or moved.
}
::ENG3_U05_L02_Q18::[MLA.ENG3.V.02] Word family: predict, dictate, diction. These words connect to saying or speaking. What does diction most likely mean in a literary discussion? {
~A building's structure#This is unrelated.
=Word choice or manner of expression#Correct. Diction connects to saying or word choice.
~A type of transportation#This is unrelated.
~A source's publication date#This is unrelated.
}
::ENG3_U05_L02_Q19::[MLA.ENG3.V.02] Sentence: The speaker's inaudible answer frustrated the audience. Prefix clue: in- can mean not; audio relates to sound. What does inaudible mean? {
=Not able to be heard#Correct. In- plus audible means not audible.
~Not able to be carried#This confuses audio with port.
~Not able to be written#This confuses audio with script.
~Not able to be trusted#This confuses audio with cred.
}
::ENG3_U05_L02_Q20::[MLA.ENG3.V.01] Context: Choose the sentence that uses derivation correctly. {
~A derivation is always an unrelated word.#This is incorrect.
~A derivation removes all meaning from a root.#This is incorrect.
=A derivation is a word formed from another word or meaningful word part.#Correct. This accurately defines derivation.
~A derivation is only a spelling mistake.#This is incorrect.
}
::ENG3_U05_L02_Q21::[MLA.ENG3.V.02] Sentence: The export of local goods helped the town economy. Root clue: port means carry; ex- can mean out. What does export mean? {
~Carry in#This would fit import more closely.
=Carry or send out#Correct. Ex- plus port supports send out.
~Write again#This connects to script and re-.
~See before#This connects to preview.
}
::ENG3_U05_L02_Q22::[MLA.ENG3.R.10] Sentence: The inscription clarified who built the bridge. Which paraphrase is best? {
~The spoken answer explained who built the bridge.#Inscription is written, not spoken.
~The portable tool explained who built the bridge.#This is unrelated.
~The visible audience explained who built the bridge.#This is unrelated.
=The written words on the bridge explained who built it.#Correct. Inscription means written or carved words.
}
::ENG3_U05_L02_Q23::[MLA.ENG3.V.02] Word family: construct, structure, instruction. What shared idea most likely connects these words? {
~Hearing#This connects to audio.
~Seeing#This connects to vis.
=Building or arranging#Correct. These words connect to building, arranging, or putting together.
~Believing#This connects to cred.
}
::ENG3_U05_L02_Q24::[MLA.ENG3.V.01] Context: Choose the sentence that best uses academic vocabulary from word-family reasoning. {
=The source has credibility because it cites interviews and data.#Correct. Credibility is used accurately.
~The source has audible because it cites interviews and data.#Audible is the wrong word.
~The source has portable because it cites interviews and data.#Portable is the wrong word.
~The source has inscription because it cites interviews and data.#Inscription is the wrong word.
}
::ENG3_U05_L02_Q25::[MLA.ENG3.V.02] Sentence: The author described the event in vivid detail. Word family: describe, description, inscription. What does described mean? {
~Carried the event away#This connects to port.
~Made the event impossible to believe#This connects to incredible.
~Made the event silent#This connects to inaudible.
=Represented the event in words#Correct. The script word family connects to writing or representing in words.
}
